- Track: `storytime_app_rebuild_20261025`.
- Phase: "Phase 4: Teacher app". Task: 4.5 (`Phase check`).
- Role: `measure-mid-red`.
- Model: `deepseek/deepseek-flash#high` (a substitution, because MiniMax reached its limit).
  Green runs on `volcengine-agent-plan/glm-5.3-flash#high`.
- `phase_base_sha`: `bfaae8905993076ca1e8a49939c400eb038fe3ae`.
- `role_base_sha`: `b1d4bc52014e5874ea66878c68ec2e48e388d927` (the HEAD at role start).
- Branch: `master`. No push.

## Scope

The orchestrator default: tasks 4.6 and 4.6a are Done (`f162e92cb`, `1d941b665`). One gate covers
the task 4.5 rows and the P4.7 rows L1 to L4, S1, and S2. This is a deviation from the plan line
that says task 4.5 "does not cover task 4.6 or task 4.6a". The plan records the deviation.

## Deliverable

`apps/storytime/__tests__/phase4-browser-gate.sh`. It adds one test file and changes no production
source, no week content, and no shipped file.

The gate enters `heavy-run.sh` itself with `HEAVY_PRIORITY=p1`. It builds the production app once
with the teacher flag not set. Then it runs three servers:

- (a) `STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES=1`, with a copy of the shipped w01 whose loops part is draft;
- (b) `STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES=1`, with an approved copy of w01 (`date` 2026-11-10, `words`
  filled), because the contract fails an approved loops part with no date or no words;
- (c) no `STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES` value in the environment at all, so the default proves itself.

The copies sit in a scratch folder under `/tmp` through `STORYTIME_CONTENT_DIR` (test strategy
P3.7). No fixture file goes into `content/`. The gate refuses to start when the shipped w01 no
longer holds a draft loops part.

The port is free and never 3005 and never 3099. The server stops by its pid file and prints
`port_closed=`. The exit trap deletes the scratch folder and the throwaway database container. The
sign-in reuses the Phase 3 gate method as it is, with the account `teach-01` (role teacher) in a
throwaway Postgres. The password stays in an environment value, and no log line prints it.

